  "body": "Integrate the tested Phase 1K-A LLM gateway, M0 Knowledge/Evidence preview and Admin foundation onto verified Phase 1H. Admin now runs inside the canonical M0 H5 shell with one React root, Router, dependency tree, build and shared session/API transport. Existing Phase 1H Rule detail/validation APIs are consumed; unavailable Rule authoring and undeployed ingestion remain disabled.\n\nThe same i18next foundation now covers zh-CN, zh-HK and en-US across M0 and Admin, with 262 stable UI keys per locale, mandatory pre-build policy and negative tests. Locale switching preserves Evidence/Citation, snapshot and query state without extra API writes; source language stays independent of UI language.\n\nDraft integration checkpoint only. Do not merge. No new migration or Phase 1I/1L Domain work.\n\n| Input | Exact SHA | Merge commit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Phase 1H main / v3.6-phase1h-pass | 700951ebb9ebdf33e399158fd3fb53bb4a6c87e7 | \u2014 |\n| B / Phase 1K-A | 45af99271559ee6fd1f652e8ad169fc9afb11c55 | 13980c65fcdb6a7b6e15e9d413ea314a277069cf |\n| C / M0 | 3f89f1e8f16402f4754b474260cb9022a4bf92c6 | fa09360f50a333e6a90e2577aa579524e89107e6 |\n| D / Admin | 22196955fb0167e3a5bce25bcdf9214f6ebeadb7 | 7ba0761c26609d0c6573005a22fcef9bab5feacf |\n\nFinal integration SHA: `6c2aacd6475af0c0533717daa54b8e48946647e1`.\n\nB \u2192 C \u2192 D merge order and focused gates were preserved. Source branches were not rebased, amended or force-pushed. Only delivery documents conflicted: B files_created_modified.md/test_result.md; D files_created_modified.md/integration_handoff.md. Both owners' original bytes remain under docs/delivery with SHA-256 proof. No executable merge conflict occurred. The loopback UAT adapter's added Rule routing was corrected to match the unchanged production app's order after real API validation.\n\nLocal validation:\n- 370 full Python tests, zero skipped/failures/errors; fresh Phase 1B\u20131H schema/runtime start-resume-retry gate PASS.\n- Architecture 118/118 covering Rules 1\u2013139; LLM boundaries 20/20; integration preservation/single-host integrity 13/13.\n- Canonical npm ci, typecheck, lint, 63 unit tests and one production build PASS; frozen API/type regeneration unchanged.\n- 36 real PostgreSQL/Redis/Chromium checks: three locales \u00d7 four scenarios repeated three times, zero retries. Knowledge/Evidence/Citation/Sufficiency/Fallback/READY, tenant A/B isolation, same-host Admin and normal-user backend denial.\n- Existing H Rule APIs exercised through the trusted session adapter; ordinary users receive 403 on privileged operations. Production authentication is not claimed.\n- Alembic head 0008_phase1h; no Alembic diff or new migration.\n\nRemote exact-head CI: **SUCCESS** for final `6c2aacd6475af0c0533717daa54b8e48946647e1`.\n- [Backend runtime/contract CI 37274812726](https://github.com/bensuen0831/crossborder-compliance-agent/actions/runs/37274812726): both jobs SUCCESS; measured annotation proves tested PR head and actual runner SHA equal the final head, pytest 370 PASS/0 skips, architecture 118/118, runtime 25/25 and Alembic 0008_phase1h.\n- [M0/Admin/multilingual CI 37274812602](https://github.com/bensuen0831/crossborder-compliance-agent/actions/runs/37274812602): frontend and real-backend-uat jobs SUCCESS, including reproducible frozen API/types, source/LLM integrity, trusted session security and three-locale browser UAT without retries.\n\nEarlier backend CI at 91cafd passed, while its frontend CI failed 5/12 browser cases; no overall PASS is claimed for that earlier head. Background session refresh now retains workspace context, with a deterministic regression. The final local matrix passes 63 unit/36 browser tests. Both final workflows explicitly checkout pull_request.head.sha.\n\nComplete changed-file inventory: [files_created_modified.md](files_created_modified.md), [machine-readable inventory](evidence/stage1-alpha/changed_files.json): 252 paths, including 56 frontend and 8 backend/Python package paths. C declared dependencies/devDependencies/engines and package-lock.json remain identical to the tested C source; package.json adds only mandatory i18n-check/build scripts; D's independent package/lock/bootstrap/tool configuration is removed and recoverable in ancestry. See [dependency integration](frontend_dependency_integration_result.md).\n\nI18N_METADATA_BACKEND_GAP remains explicit: current backend-managed business names render verbatim; no second frontend business translation registry was invented. Metadata/registry owners (OTHER), Knowledge (M1) and production contract rollout own the missing localized metadata. See [multilingual proof](multilingual_frontend_result.md).\n\nProduction identity/CSRF, fine-grained contextual/Knowledge RBAC, ingestion storage/worker deployment, Knowledge history/binary linkage/security metadata, generic metadata list/payload/version/status/catalog, recovery and full Rule authoring remain assigned upstream gaps. The local demo uses explicit loopback-only synthetic trusted sessions; the frontend does not authorize callers. See [gap owners](admin_backend_gap_report.md), [security proof](security_integration_result.md), [test evidence](test_result.md), [design](stage1_alpha_integration_design.md) and [handoff](stage1_alpha_integration_handoff.md).\n",
